// Build settings that are safe to commit.
//
// The `?` on the include makes a missing Secrets.xcconfig a no-op rather than a build error,
// so a fresh checkout builds and runs on local data with nothing configured. Quokka needs no
// keys today -- every thumbnail endpoint it uses is public -- and this exists so that stays
// true by default if one is ever added.
// The worker that serves the transcript ladder's config. Not a secret -- it is a public host,
// compiled into the app either way -- so it lives here, and Secrets.xcconfig (included below)
// can still point a build somewhere else. Host only: `//` starts a comment in an xcconfig.
QUOKKA_WORKER_HOST = quokka.matthew-parkk0.workers.dev

#include? "Secrets.xcconfig"
